## Non-Negotiable Coding Conventions
- No unwrap() or expect() outside #[test] blocks or the cli crate's main().
- thiserror for library-crate error types; anyhow only at the cli binary boundary.
- Every public function in ingest-core, contention, and ohlcv has at least one unit test.
- Run `cargo clippy` and fix warnings before considering any task done.
- contention and ohlcv must stay zero-I/O — do not add database or network imports to them.

## First Session Checklist
1. `cargo build` at the workspace root — fix whatever doesn't compile (expect some errors; this
   was hand-written without a compiler checking it).
2. `cargo test -p contention -p ohlcv` — these should pass immediately since the logic was
   verified in Python first; if they don't, the transcription (not the algorithm) has a bug.
3. Get a Helius API key, hit `getBlock` once manually, compare the raw JSON against
   `ingest-core/src/rpc_client.rs`'s `Raw*` structs, fix mismatches.
4. Build out the real bounded-channel pipeline in `cli/main.rs` for FR-5.1.
5. Finish `build_and_store_candles` in `cli/main.rs`.
